      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the area of the shaded region in Wei's logo, which consists of squares and circles. Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Determine the side length of the square and the radius of the circles:**\n   The side length of the square is given as 20 inches. Since the circles are tangent to two sides of the square and their adjacent circles, the diameter of each circle is equal to the side length of the smaller square formed by the centers of the circles. This smaller square has a side length of \\(2 \\times 1 = 2\\) inches (because the circles are tangent to the sides of the square).\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the square:**\n   The area of the square is the side length squared:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the square} = 20^2 = 400 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   The shaded area is the area of the square minus the area of the 3 smaller circles (since the circles are tangent to each other and form a smaller square inside the larger square).\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one circle:**\n   The radius of each circle is \\(1\\) inch. The area of one circle is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one circle} = \\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   Since there are 3 circles, the total area of the circles is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the circles} = 3\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the shaded area is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Shaded area} = 400 - 3\\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the number of square inches that will be shaded is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{400 - 3\\pi}\n\\]",
